# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the host KV tier SHIP-CANDIDATE gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/prefix-tiers and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed tp4/prefix-tiers head
# (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-tier-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# TQ1 (STOP): the PER-TENANT QUOTA gate (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-quota, scenario tier_quota; docs/prefix-store-hygiene.md "Tenant quotas") on the ship candidate's gate-only audit twin c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tierfx-audit. Two arms, two boots, the same
# scenario: tenant B builds a session (56k) and tenant A (one salt) a smaller one (32k); tenant A floods the device pool with fresh prompts totalling the pool and one more flood; then B RETURNS and
# then A, each sent as a hit and then as its cold twin under a fresh salt and compared in full (a strict pair). quota-control is the twin as it is (no quota): the flood must reach B (restored from
# host RAM or cold), else the arm proves nothing. quota-isolated is the same twin with the quota env the gate derives (QWEN_PREFIX_TENANT_QUOTA_DEVICE_CAP_TOKENS=262144, _DEVICE_FLOOR_TOKENS=65536,
# _HOST_CAP_GIB=12, _HOST_FLOOR_GIB=4: the floor above B's session, the cap well under the pool): B's return must be a DEVICE-RESIDENT hit (the oracle's Q, no 'host tier restore' line for its request) while
# tenant A, over its cap, evicted its own blocks. READ: both arms PASS; in the isolated arm the install line 'tenant quota on device_cap_tokens=... device=1 host=1', quota_dev_evictions_own above 0 (the cap
# bit) and quota_host_evictions_own above 0 (the host cap bit), quota_dev_floor_overrides 0 (an override voids the arm: NOT_EXERCISED), the tier's failure counters ZERO, and the lines 'tenant B returned: Q=
# ... device-resident'; all four pairs IDENTICAL. Then python3 scripts/ci/tier_concurrent_compare.py --quota <results>/quota-control <results>/quota-isolated: both tenants' returning answers IDENTICAL
# across the arms (the quota may move which blocks the pool keeps, never an answer). Counters are aggregates: no tenant, salt or digest is exported or logged. Unqualified: a measurement, never evidence.
# Duration (estimate; the floods at the production pool are the unmeasured part, two arms each with a boot): 120 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-tier-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-quota
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-tierfx-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=240
